  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{u}}=\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{j}}, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}=\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-\\hat{\\mathrm{j}}$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{w}}=\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+3 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}$. If $\\hat{\\mathrm{n}}$ is a unit vector such that $\\vec{u} \\cdot \\hat{n}=0$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}} \\cdot \\hat{\\mathrm{n}}=0$, then $|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{w}} \\cdot \\hat{\\mathrm{n}}|$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n3\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n2",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{n}}$ is perpendicular $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{u}}$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{n}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{u}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}$\n$\\hat{\\mathrm{n}}=\\frac{\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathrm{i} & \\mathrm{j} & \\mathrm{k} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right|}{\\sqrt{2} \\times \\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}}{2}=-\\hat{\\mathrm{k}}$\n$|\\vec{\\omega} \\cdot \\hat{n}|=|(\\mathrm{i}+2 \\mathrm{j}+3 \\mathrm{k}) \\cdot(-\\mathrm{k})|=|-3|=3$"
  }
}